# Everything Vercel does not need in order to serve site/.
#
# The deploy is static files and nothing else: no build step, no dependencies,
# no runtime. Uploading package.json in particular is not merely wasteful —
# it has a `build` script that runs tsdown over the CLI, and Vercel's zero-config
# detection would find it and try to run it. Keeping it out is what makes the
# project read as static.
#
# This is a deny list rather than `*` plus a negation for site/, because a
# negation Vercel does not honour fails by uploading nothing, while a deny list
# that falls behind fails by uploading a few files too many.

# The tool itself
src/
dist/
test/
scripts/
action.yml

# Toolchain and config
package.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
tsconfig.json
tsdown.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
driftwatch.config.ts
driftwatch.docs.config.ts
.oxlintrc.json
.prettierrc.json
.prettierignore
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Documentation and repository furniture
docs/
README.md
AGENTS.md
PRODUCT.md
LICENSE
.github/
.gitignore
.scratch/

# Local noise
.DS_Store
